# Store compliance — web pages + in-app delete (required every build)

Before any **release build** (AAB, IPA, or store submission), ensure all items below exist. Do not ship without them.

## Required website files (separate HTML per page)

Maintain under `website/` and deploy to **gh-pages** (not `main` root):

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `website/support.html` | Support + download links (web, Android, iOS) |
| `website/privacy.html` | Privacy policy (Google Play / App Store URL) |
| `website/delete-account.html` | Delete-account URL for Play Console |

Rules for HTML:
- Use **HTTPS** links only in production URLs (`https://zub165.github.io/LocalNewsBreaker/...`)
- One topic per file — no monolithic single-page app for legal/support content
- Contact email: **zub165@yahoo.com**
- `delete-account.html` must document the **built-in app** Delete Account flow first

After editing `website/`, copy to `gh-pages` branch root and push; trigger GitHub Pages rebuild.

## Required in-app features (Flutter)

In `mobile/lib/main.dart` (or extracted auth module):

1. **Account / profile UI** reachable from the app (e.g. World tab → profile icon)
2. **Delete Account** button that calls backend `DELETE /api/v1/users/me/` via `Api.deleteAccount()`
3. Clear user feedback on success (SnackBar) and session cleared locally

Do not remove Delete Account when refactoring auth.

## Pre-build verification (mandatory)

Run before `flutter build appbundle` or `flutter build ipa`:

```bash
cd mobile && bash tool/verify_store_compliance.sh
```

Fix all failures before building release artifacts.

## Release build commands (include API URL)

```bash
cd mobile
bash tool/verify_store_compliance.sh
flutter build appbundle --release --dart-define=API_BASE_URL=https://citizen-api.mywaitime.com
flutter build ipa --release --dart-define=API_BASE_URL=https://citizen-api.mywaitime.com
```

